architect › Job done.

**What changed:**
- `src/limiter.ts` — Token-bucket `RateLimiter`: private `tokens`/`last` state seeded full at construction time from the injected `now()`, a private continuous `refill()` (elapsed ms ÷ 1000 × refillPerSecond, clamped at capacity), `tryTake(n)` refusing `n > capacity` (and negative) before touching the bucket and otherwise taking all-or-nothing, and a lazy `available` getter that refills to the current time and returns the raw fractional count. No rounding anywhere.
- `src/limiter.test.ts` — 9 tests total: the original "starts full" plus drain/refill against a controlled clock, capacity clamp on long waits, `n > capacity` refused even when full, all-or-nothing behavior, fractional take, continuous refill across successive takes, and a default-clock smoke test.

